{
  "name": "YouTube video to blog draft in Google Docs",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## YouTube video to blog draft in Google Docs\n\n**What it does**\nWhen your channel publishes a new video, it grabs the transcript (or the video description if no transcript is available), has OpenAI turn it into a structured blog draft, and saves it as a new Google Doc in your drafts folder. You edit and publish.\n\n**You need**\nOpenAI and Google Docs credentials, a free YouTube Data API key, and optionally a transcript API (any service that returns a video's transcript as text over HTTP).\n\n**Setup**\n1. Put your channel ID in the feed URL of **New video on the channel**.\n2. Create two Query Auth credentials: `YouTube Data API key` (name `key`) and, if you use one, `Transcript API key` (see the yellow note).\n3. Pick the Drive folder in **Create the draft doc**, connect credentials, activate.\n\nBuilt by AI Strike Force, aistrikeforce.com",
        "height": 680,
        "width": 580
      },
      "id": "2be07b24-c401-527a-a11f-a05b3cf6739d",
      "name": "YouTube video to blog draft in Google Docs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -640,
        -100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Edit me\nReplace YOUR_CHANNEL_ID in the feed URL. It is the `UC...` ID on your channel's About page (Share channel, Copy channel ID).",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 260,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "ba46d48c-1fa0-59d4-a374-cd3caf74faa4",
      "name": "Edit me: channel",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Edit me: transcript\nPoint **Fetch the transcript** at your transcript API and match its auth. The next node reads `text`, `transcript` or `content` from the response. No transcript service? Select the node and press D to disable it: the video description is used instead. If the service is down, the node fails quietly and the description is used too.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "5f8e118d-8d69-57f2-8b14-72739805f36d",
      "name": "Edit me: transcript source",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        440,
        -20
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Edit me\nPick the Google Drive folder for drafts. Docs are titled `DRAFT: <post title>`.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "9edb10c0-ad23-5baa-9eae-4f162b96bb20",
      "name": "Edit me: folder",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1540,
        40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "pollTimes": {
          "item": [
            {
              "mode": "everyHour"
            }
          ]
        },
        "feedUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/feeds/videos.xml?channel_id=YOUR_CHANNEL_ID"
      },
      "id": "10bd93f5-47ad-5734-8401-79a05b059b67",
      "name": "New video on the channel",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.rssFeedReadTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "6a907396-934c-573c-a313-9b27835b647f",
              "name": "video_id",
              "value": "={{ String($json.id || '').replace('yt:video:', '') || (String($json.link).split('v=')[1] || '').split('&')[0] }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "4f4707df-4945-5bbb-89e5-5c8171b272c5",
              "name": "title",
              "value": "={{ $json.title }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "2f24daef-6ecc-5030-bb94-a99db22bbfc4",
              "name": "link",
              "value": "={{ $json.link }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "2a1782cc-b45e-591d-b1e1-d0df92be38df",
      "name": "Get the video ID",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        220,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://your-transcript-service.example.com/transcript",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpQueryAuth",
        "sendQuery": true,
        "queryParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "video_id",
              "value": "={{ $json.video_id }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "timeout": 60000
        }
      },
      "id": "c6c8f23f-fb47-55fe-b566-07a5b4857790",
      "name": "Fetch the transcript",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        440,
        300
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "httpQueryAuth": {
          "name": "Transcript API key"
        }
      },
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://www.googleapis.com/youtube/v3/videos",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpQueryAuth",
        "sendQuery": true,
        "queryParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "part",
              "value": "snippet"
            },
            {
              "name": "id",
              "value": "={{ $('Get the video ID').item.json.video_id }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "timeout": 20000
        }
      },
      "id": "54dc0919-f55b-5c52-bd40-832bab7b0b67",
      "name": "Fetch the video description",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        660,
        300
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "httpQueryAuth": {
          "name": "YouTube Data API key"
        }
      },
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "2795ee3a-c40d-576e-8b16-866ee8d4c012",
              "name": "title",
              "value": "={{ $('Get the video ID').item.json.title }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "34cf09b7-c81e-5c04-aa9d-fdf40dbaf3cf",
              "name": "link",
              "value": "={{ $('Get the video ID').item.json.link }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "12bd6151-e54e-5bd8-853a-eef783db32e5",
              "name": "transcript",
              "value": "={{ String($('Fetch the transcript').item.json.text || $('Fetch the transcript').item.json.transcript || $('Fetch the transcript').item.json.content || '').trim() }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "cdd20d35-25a6-567a-8ae1-0a549a2d9ead",
              "name": "description",
              "value": "={{ String($json.items?.[0]?.snippet?.description || '').trim() }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "8413545b-4c7a-5c79-bb42-cea8899a155f",
              "name": "source_type",
              "value": "={{ String($('Fetch the transcript').item.json.text || $('Fetch the transcript').item.json.transcript || $('Fetch the transcript').item.json.content || '').trim().length > 300 ? 'transcript' : 'description' }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "fece90b0-5018-5f84-875f-ffc85e1297d3",
      "name": "Pick the source text",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        880,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Video title: {{ $json.title }}\nVideo link: {{ $json.link }}\nSource type: {{ $json.source_type }}\n\nSource text:\n{{ ($json.source_type === 'transcript' ? $json.transcript : $json.description).slice(0, 40000) }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You turn YouTube videos into blog post drafts for [YOUR COMPANY]'s website. Readers: [YOUR AUDIENCE].\n\nRules:\n- Use only what the source says. Do not add facts, numbers, tools or quotes that are not in it.\n- If the source type is \"description\", the source is short: write a short post (200 to 400 words) and do not pad it.\n- If it is a transcript, write 700 to 1200 words, cut the filler and spoken tics, and keep the speaker's actual advice and examples.\n- Structure the body in Markdown: a two or three sentence intro, H2 sections, short paragraphs, a short \"Key takeaways\" list, and a closing line that links to the video.\n- Plain, direct language. No em dashes, no \"in today's world\", no \"let's dive in\".\n- title: under 60 characters, says what the reader gets. meta_description: under 155 characters."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "id": "ef732ff7-c72d-5b74-a42c-77384066d784",
      "name": "Write the blog draft",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        1100,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-4.1-mini",
          "cachedResultName": "gpt-4.1-mini"
        },
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.5
        }
      },
      "id": "49d5de1b-2eae-58a2-9a27-2a853eae1d90",
      "name": "OpenAI Chat Model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        1040,
        520
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "name": "OpenAI account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "schemaType": "fromJson",
        "jsonSchemaExample": "{\n  \"title\": \"How to answer every lead in under 5 minutes\",\n  \"meta_description\": \"A simple setup that texts, emails and alerts your team the moment a lead comes in.\",\n  \"body\": \"Most leads go cold within the first hour...\\n\\n## Why speed matters\\n...\"\n}",
        "autoFix": false
      },
      "id": "eb1c2076-6acc-57cd-ac14-031b1db7938b",
      "name": "Title, meta and body",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        1220,
        520
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "create",
        "driveId": "myDrive",
        "folderId": "YOUR_FOLDER_ID",
        "title": "=DRAFT: {{ $json.output.title }}"
      },
      "id": "0b5cf20f-cc6c-5508-a321-ace43144e16c",
      "name": "Create the draft doc",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleDocs",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1540,
        300
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "googleDocsOAuth2Api": {
          "name": "Google Docs account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "update",
        "documentURL": "={{ $json.id }}",
        "actionsUi": {
          "actionFields": [
            {
              "action": "insert",
              "object": "text",
              "text": "=Title: {{ $('Write the blog draft').item.json.output.title }}\nMeta description: {{ $('Write the blog draft').item.json.output.meta_description }}\nSource video: {{ $('Pick the source text').item.json.link }} (written from the {{ $('Pick the source text').item.json.source_type }})\n\n{{ $('Write the blog draft').item.json.output.body }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "f80be611-f443-5054-9454-9ceec73d8369",
      "name": "Write the draft into the doc",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleDocs",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1760,
        300
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "googleDocsOAuth2Api": {
          "name": "Google Docs account"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
